{"tool_name":"rnainteract","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"rnainteract","home":"http://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/RNAinteract.html","license":"Artistic-2.0","summary":"This tool estimates genetic interactions from multi-dimensional read-outs like features extracted from images. The screen is assumed to be performed in multi-well plates or similar designs. Starting from a list of features (e.g. cell number, area, fluorescence intensity) per well, genetic interactions are estimated. The packages provides functions for reporting interacting gene pairs, plotting heatmaps and double RNAi plots. An HTML report can be written for quality control and analysis.","addition_date":"2017-01-17T14:59:38Z","last_update_date":"2018-12-30T15:52:35Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library"],"version":["1.22.0"],"collections":["BioConductor"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:rnainteract","credit":[{"email":"b.fischer@dkfz.de","name":"Bernd Fischer","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0001-9437-2099","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/RNAinteract.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Nucleic acid features","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1276"},"format":[{"term":"Image format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3547"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0337"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Report","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2048"},"format":[{"term":"HTML","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2331"}]}]}],"name":"RNAinteract","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"bioconductor_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/nmeth.1581","metadata":{"abstract":"The analysis of synthetic genetic interaction networks can reveal how biological systems achieve a high level of complexity with a limited repertoire of components. Studies in yeast and bacteria have taken advantage of collections of deletion strains to construct matrices of quantitative interaction profiles and infer gene function. Yet comparable approaches in higher organisms have been difficult to implement in a robust manner. Here we report a method to identify genetic interactions in tissue culture cells through RNAi. By performing more than 70,000 pairwise perturbations of signaling factors, we identified >600 interactions affecting different quantitative phenotypes of Drosophila melanogaster cells. Computational analysis of this interaction matrix allowed us to reconstruct signaling pathways and identify a conserved regulator of Ras-MAPK signaling. Large-scale genetic interaction mapping by RNAi is a versatile, scalable approach for revealing gene function and the connectivity of cellular networks. \u00a9 2011 Nature America, Inc. All rights reserved.","authors":[{"name":"Axelsson E."},{"name":"Boutros M."},{"name":"Fischer B."},{"name":"Horn T."},{"name":"Huber W."},{"name":"Sandmann T."}],"citationCount":143,"date":"2011-04-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nature Methods","title":"Mapping of signaling networks through synthetic genetic interaction analysis by RNAi"},"pmid":"21378980","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Bioinformatics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0091"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"RNAinteract","home":"https://bio.tools/rnainteract","license":"Artistic-2.0","version":"1.22.0","summary":"This tool estimates genetic interactions from multi-dimensional read-outs like features extracted from images. The screen is assumed to be performed in multi-well plates or similar designs. Starting from a list of features (e.g. cell number, area, fluorescence intensity) per well, genetic interactions are estimated. The packages provides functions for reporting interacting gene pairs, plotting heatmaps and double RNAi plots. An HTML report can be written for quality control and analysis."